Instructions:

1)  mkdir CASE_tools
2)  cd CASE_tools
3)  git clone https://github.com/CESM-Development/CESM_CASE_MANAGEMENT_TOOLS -b tibetPlateau  tibetPlateau
4)  cd tibetPlateau/scripts

The directory should contain a script to create your new case: create_b.e21.BHIST.f09_g17.Tibet-1.50.001


Background:  
This is a project with Aixue Hu and his Chinese visitor, Ruizao.  They are testing the effect of the Tibetan Plateau on the Asian monsoon by running sensitivity tests, systematically raising/lowering the height of the Plateau.   This case is the 5th and final test and it increases the height of the plateau by 50% (!!).  Unfortunately, even though we taper the elevation, the sudden height increase crashes the model.  So they have come up with a way to slowly adjust the elevation by gradually imposing the increase, 5% at a time.  

Procedure:
The way it works is that you will run 10 years, one year at a time.  After each year, you will change the topography forcing by modifying user_nl_cam.

